<title>SOUTH AFRICA: FNB signs 80 mln rand EIB funding facility.</title>
<headline>FNB signs 80 mln rand EIB funding facility.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's First National Bank Ltd announced on Thursday it had signed an 80 million rand infrastructure finance facility with the European Investment Bank (EIB).</p>
<p>The agreement would allow First National to access both fixed and variable funding in all major currencies for up to 15 years for infrastructure projects, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agreement marked the first time a private sector funding facility had been entered into by the EIB in South Africa.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
